This is the README file for kbsh.
K3BACON SHELL (kbsh) is a lightweight UNIX shell. It controls interaction
between the user and the operating system via command line.

	Copyright (C) 2011, 2012 Zack Parsons <k3bacon@gmail.com>

	Copying and distribution of this file, with or without modification,
	are permitted in any medium without royalty provided the copyright
	notice and this notice are preserved.

Build and install now use the top-level Makefile (no autotools required):

	make
	make test
	make install PREFIX=$HOME/.local

Current development target:

	0.3.0-dev

Current devel branch coverage includes:

- parameter expansion
- pipelines and exit-status propagation
- basic file redirection (`>`, `>>`, `<`, `2>`, `2>&1`)
- custom interactive line editing
- early command substitution (`$()`)

Version support:

- Default version comes from `./VERSION`.
- Override per build with `make VERSION=0.1.1`.
- Check effective version with `make version`.

Autotools files have been removed from this repository.

Source Code: https://github.com/zstuartp/kbsh/

Email: parsons.zackary@gmail.com

